# What NOT to put on GitHub.
#
# The site itself is small — two files and about 79 photographs. The rest
# of this folder is 400MB of camera originals, old experiments and drafts.
# Keeping those out means the repository stays fast to clone and the
# history stays readable.

# ---- generated ----
# PUBLISH/ is built by publish.ps1 from the files that ARE tracked, so
# committing it would store the same photographs twice.
PUBLISH/

# ---- the zips ----
# Snapshots of the repository. Committing a zip of the repo INTO the repo
# doubles its size every time.
*.zip

# ---- camera originals and staging folders ----
# The working `images/` folder is tracked; these are the unedited sources
# and holding areas it was built from.
NEW IMAGES/
photos for website/
cover photos/
random stuff/
traditional potraits/
textures/
3D GENERATION/
CAM EXPERIMENT/

# ---- old versions and experiments ----
# Kept on disk, but they are not the site and clutter the history.
V1-*.html
V2-BEFORE-3D.html
NOIR-BLANC-*.html
*-SAMPLE.html
*-STUDY.html
*-CUSTOM.html
BOXES-*.html
HERO-*.html
COVER-TITLE.html
GRID-*.html
SCROLL-SAMPLE.html
TYPE-STUDY.html
MOBILE-SAMPLE.html
PARKED-*.txt
*.bak

# ---- editor and OS noise ----
.claude/
.vscode/
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.tmp
